\begin{ex}{Min Cost Network Flow}{}
\label{ex:min-cost-flow-picture}
\stars{2} Use the picture below to formulate the corresponding capacitated min cost network flow.  Each arc is labeled with its capacity (black) and its per-unit cost ({\color{red}red}); the blue number at each node is its net demand (positive = demand, negative = supply).  Solve this problem using Excel.  As a check, the minimum cost is $67$.
% NOTE (2026-07-13, solutions-manual QA): arc (v2,v1) capacity changed 1 -> 4.
% With capacity 1 the instance was infeasible under either sign convention:
% node v1 demands 6 units but its maximum net inflow was x_{v5,v1} + x_{v2,v1}
% <= 2 + 1 = 3 (v5 supplies only 2).  With capacity 4 the instance is feasible
% (tightly: every feasible flow has x_{v5,v1} = 2, x_{v2,v1} = 4) and the
% optimal cost is 67, verified with scipy.linprog.

